WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Crumbling, spectral archive — shelves of glowing, fading memory-shards., tense.

2
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.300 align:center
Lyra: Too fast! They're everywhere!

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.600 align:center
Echo Shard: Redundant. Unnecessary.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.900 align:center
Lyra: Almost there. Just... one more shelf.

5
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.200 align:center
Kael: The path… it shifts.

6
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.500 align:center
Lyra: Got it! Navigation Shard secured!

7
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:24.800 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in A narrow, unstable memory-corridor within the archive, choked with debris., urgent.

8
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.100 align:center
Lyra: Crumbling! It's all falling apart!

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.400 align:center
Kael: Hold it... or lose it.

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.700 align:center
Lyra: No! This one... it's important!

11
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.000 align:center
Echo Shard: Inefficient. Release.

12
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.300 align:center
Lyra: Damn it! Shield!

13
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.600 align:center
Lyra: Cracked... it's cracked.

14
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:44.900 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in A momentarily stable, but still decaying, memory-chamber, filled with ghostly, fading projections., dread.

15
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.200 align:center
Lyra: Safe... for now. What was that?

16
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.500 align:center
Kael: The weave... I know this.

17
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.800 align:center
Lyra: Kael? What do you mean?

18
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.100 align:center
Kael: A Warning Shard... a familiar pattern.

19
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.400 align:center
Lyra: Familiar to who? To you?

20
00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:04.700 align:center
♪ at dawn, in A bridge or pathway made of shimmering memory-strands, actively dissolving into a void., desperate.

21
00:01:04.1000 --> 00:01:05.1000 align:center
Lyra: It's dissolving! Faster!

22
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.300 align:center
Loom of Oblivion: Disorder becomes order.

23
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.600 align:center
Lyra: Can't look down! Just move!

24
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.900 align:center
Lyra: A Purpose Shard! Mine!

25
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:19.200 align:center
♪ in broad daylight, in A memory-chamber where illusions play on Lyra's past, shifting and distorting., tense.

26
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.500 align:center
Lyra: No... that's not real. It can't be.

27
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.800 align:center
Illusion (Voice): You chose this. You left them.

28
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.100 align:center
Lyra: Lies! Kael, what is this?

29
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.400 align:center
Kael: They know... what you hide.

30
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.700 align:center
Lyra: Help me! Don't let me drown here!

31
00:01:33.1000 --> 00:01:41.1000 align:center
♪ in broad daylight, in A section of memory being actively 'purified' by the Loom, glowing with destructive energy., dread.

32
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.300 align:center
Lyra: Burning... everything lost.

33
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.600 align:center
Loom of Oblivion: Waste becomes purity. Embrace clarity.

34
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.900 align:center
Lyra: This isn't purity! It's annihilation!

35
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.200 align:center
Kael: They believe... they protect.

36
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:59.500 align:center
♪ at dusk, in A locked memory-gate, requiring a specific 'key' memory to open, with Silence entities closing in., desperate.

37
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.800 align:center
Lyra: Locked! I need a key.

38
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.100 align:center
Echo Shard: Inefficient. Surrender.

39
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.400 align:center
Lyra: No... not this one. I can't.

40
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.700 align:center
Kael: You must. Or perish.

41
00:02:07.1000 --> 00:02:09.1000 align:center
Lyra: Which one?! How do I choose?

42
00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:18.300 align:center
♪ at dusk, in A chamber where the Loom's threads are visibly active, trying to ensnare Lyra., dread.

43
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.600 align:center
Lyra: Pulling me in! Can't break free!

44
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.900 align:center
Loom of Oblivion: Join the collective. Find peace.

45
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.200 align:center
Lyra: No! I won't! Not yet!

46
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.500 align:center
Kael: The current... it's strong.

47
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:38.800 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in The very core of the memory-world, where the 'Compass Shard' is being devoured by the Loom of Oblivion., desperate.

48
00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.100 align:center
Lyra: The Compass! It's almost gone!

49
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.400 align:center
Echo Shard: Pointless. Inevitable.

50
00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.700 align:center
Lyra: Not without a fight! Get back!

51
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.000 align:center
Loom of Oblivion: Return to source.

52
00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:54.300 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in Same as S09, the Loom is actively consuming the 'Compass Shard'., desperate.

53
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.600 align:center
Lyra: I can't lose it! Not my compass!

54
00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.900 align:center
Kael: A greater loss... to hold back.

55
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.200 align:center
Lyra: This one... my mother's laugh!

56
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.500 align:center
Loom of Oblivion: Resistance is futile.

57
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.800 align:center
Lyra: Forgive me! Forgive me!

58
00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:15.100 align:center
♪ under the cover of darkness, in The empty space where the 'Compass Shard' was, the Loom's presence overwhelming., dread.

59
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.400 align:center
Lyra: It's gone... I lost it.

60
00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.700 align:center
Kael: A heavy cost... for survival.

61
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.000 align:center
Loom of Oblivion: The path is clear now.

62
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.300 align:center
Loom of Oblivion: Next, the Core. Your very essence.

63
00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.600 align:center
Lyra: My... my core?
